ENVIRONMENT CONSTRAINT (not a NEARS-2552 defect): the emulator's own FCM/Play-Services
registration call failed live during login with SERVICE_NOT_AVAILABLE (see
ac1-live-login-flow.log) -- this sandboxed emulator has no working path to Google's FCM
registration/delivery infrastructure (adb shell ping to 8.8.8.8/google.com hung
indefinitely, never resolved). The token found in the DB is a stale/cached value from
an earlier session's client-side cache, not a token freshly registered in this run --
Google's 404 (UNREGISTERED) on send is consistent with that. Confirmed no
notification arrived device-side: no FirebaseMessagingService/onMessageReceived log
line, and `dumpsys notification` shows zero active notifications for com.izzes.nears
after the send attempt.

CONCLUSION: AC3's on-device delivery leg is UNVERIFIABLE in this sandbox (infra
limitation, not a code defect). What IS confirmed live: the full send pipeline works
end-to-end through Google's own accept/reject decision (positive control above), and
the mechanism this fix touches -- cm-firebase-token accepting and persisting the
client's token server-side -- is proven working (AC1 DB-persistence evidence). The
persisted token is written and read back byte-identical to what the app sent,
regardless of downstream FCM deliverability.
